# Part 3: What you will see

**Operators** receive a guided path instead of a 72-item list, and a written definition for every field. The system presents the questions; the operator records what is known. Incident creation is faster, and no situation requires a choice between two equally defensible types.

**Duty officers and command** receive a consistent common operating picture. The same situation is recorded the same way regardless of who entered it or on which shift. Status, type, and outcome each carry a single meaning, so the picture can be read consistently.

**Our leadership and our services** receive reporting that can be relied upon. Season data for SLSA, councils, LSV, and our clubs ceases to be a manual interrogation exercise for the EMCaR team and becomes a query. Trends become visible, and questions are answered directly from the data. That reliability compounds into everything the data touches: how we structure our services, how we support our members, and how we make the case for funding.

Together with the first aid form work, this presents a cohesive picture of operational data done properly, a piece of work LSV can be proud of and share with the other states as industry-leading.

